  "geometry_notes": "One panel only, centered. Beaker: open cylinder radius 1.2, height 3.0, wall thickness ~0.06, base at y=0, centered at origin; small pour spout on the upper LEFT rim. Liquid: cylinder radius 1.14, top surface at y=1.95 (≈65% fill) at full state; a slightly brighter cyan band 0.12 tall marks the meniscus. Electrodes: flat plates 0.9 (X) × 1.9 (Y) × 0.04 (Z), centered at x=-0.55 and x=+0.55, z=0, top edge at y=2.35 so ~0.4 stands above the liquid; each plate tilted ~8° about the Y axis (left plate rotated so its right face turns toward the viewer, right plate mirrored) and ~4° about Z, exactly as in the source where both plates lean. Grey stems: cylinders radius 0.03 from each plate top up to y=3.6. Wall outlet: grey plate 0.5×0.7 at x=-3.4, y=3.3, with black two-prong plug body 0.35×0.25. Light bulb: glass sphere radius 0.42 centered at x=+2.6, y=4.3, with ribbed screw base 0.3 tall below it; filament = two thin posts plus a coil at the sphere center. Wires: thick black tubes (radius 0.035) drawn as smooth catmull-rom arcs — left electrode stem up to (-1.1, 3.9) then sweeping left-down to the plug; plug to bulb base as one long shallow arc peaking near y=4.4; bulb base down to right electrode stem. Particles: spheres radius 0.11, green #7CC423 with darker #4E8C12 rim; neutral molecule = two spheres fused at 0.16 separation; ions = single spheres with white '+' or '−' glyph. Arrows: black, length 0.5–0.9, radius 0.015, drawn horizontally from the ion toward its target plate (cations → left/− plate, anions → right/+ plate). Particle counts at concentration 0.5: ethanol = 5 neutral dumbbells, 0 ions, no arrows; KCl = 0 dumbbells, 6 ions (3 '+' moving left, 3 '−' moving right) all with arrows; acetic acid = 3 dumbbells plus 2 ions (one '+' with left arrow, one '−' with right arrow). Scale all counts linearly with the concentration slider (0→0 particles, 1.0→double the listed counts). Colors: beaker glass #BFD8DC at ~25% opacity with white specular highlight stripes, solution #A9E2EC at ~45% opacity, electrodes grey gradient #B8B8B8→#8E8E8E with a lighter top bevel, '−' sign black, '+' sign red #E04B3C, wires/plug black #1A1A1A, socket plate grey #8A8A8A, bulb glass #EDF2F4 at 40% opacity, filament orange #F0A030, glow halo #FFE34D. Bulb brightness model: brightness = degreeOfDissociation × concentration, with degreeOfDissociation = 0 (ethanol), 1.0 (KCl), 0.12 (acetic acid); map to emissive intensity and halo radius (0 = fully dark grey filament, 1 = bright yellow with 1.6× halo). Caption text sits centered below the beaker at y≈-0.8 in two lines, black sans-serif.",
  "notes": "Three.js: beaker and liquid as MeshPhysicalMaterial with transmission/transparency, depthWrite false and renderOrder set so the ions inside remain visible through the front wall; render inner liquid before glass. Electrode plates as thin BoxGeometry; '+'/'−' glyphs as CanvasTexture decals on the plate faces so they stay flat on the tilted surfaces. Wires via TubeGeometry along CatmullRomCurve3 control points. Bulb glow = emissive filament plus an additive sprite halo whose opacity/scale lerp with brightness; also drive a small PointLight at the bulb so the glow spills subtly onto the scene. Ion animation: each ion advances along ±X toward its target plate at constant speed, fades out on contact and respawns near the opposite side; neutral dumbbells get slow Brownian jitter plus gentle rotation and never translate directionally. Arrow meshes are children of their ion and are hidden for neutral molecules. Toggle swaps particle rosters with a short crossfade rather than a hard cut. Caption rendered as an HTML overlay or CanvasTexture sprite so text stays crisp. Keep orbit limited (azimuth ±40°, elevation 5°–45°) so the figure never loses its recognizable front-three-quarter reading."
